    {
      "title": "All smiles in Strasbourg but uncertainty clouds Canada’s EU membership plan",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/17/smiles-strasbourg-uncertainty-canada-eu-membership-plan-mark-carney",
      "description": "<p>Although Mark Carney welcomed offer to become bloc’s first associate member, no one seems to know what that means</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/sep/17/donald-trump-eu-european-union-mark-carney-canada-associate-membership-tariffs-threats-germany-merz-latest-news-updates\">Europe live – latest updates</a></p></li></ul><p>Mark Carney received a rapturous reception in the European parliament when he gave his speech on Thursday welcoming a proposal for Canada to become the EU’s first-ever associate member.</p><p>Politicians queued to shake his hand and take selfies. One described the speech as a historic moment. “Europe has extended a hand, and Canada has taken it,” said the German Green MEP Terry Reintke, who borrowed a Canadian ice hockey shirt for the occasion.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/17/smiles-strasbourg-uncertainty-canada-eu-membership-plan-mark-carney\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-17T15:46:15"
    },
    {
      "title": "Taking on Trump: Canada and EU forge closer ties – The Latest",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/news/audio/2026/sep/17/taking-on-trump-canada-and-eu-forge-closer-ties-the-latest",
      "description": "<p>Canadian prime minister, Mark Carney, has welcomed the EU’s proposal for Canada to become the bloc’s first ‘associate member’, despite threats from Donald Trump over the plan. The US president said Washington could impose ‘very serious tariffs’ or halt trade if the EU went ahead with the idea. But in a defiant speech to the European parliament, Carney called for ‘deep cooperation’ and said polling showed the overwhelming majority of Canadians supported closer ties with Europe. Lucy Hough speaks to Europe correspondent Jon Henley <strong>– </strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@todayinfocuspodcast\">watch on YouTube</a></p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/news/audio/2026/sep/17/taking-on-trump-canada-and-eu-forge-closer-ties-the-latest\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-17T18:22:14"
    },
    {
      "title": "Poland warns Russia planning ‘hybrid strikes’ against countries supporting Ukraine – as it happened",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/sep/17/donald-trump-eu-european-union-mark-carney-canada-associate-membership-tariffs-threats-germany-merz-latest-news-updates",
      "description": "<p>This blog is now closed</p><p>Meanwhile, we are getting some interesting lines from Paris that <strong>the French president, Emmanuel Macron, convened the chiefs ⁠of ⁠the ​different political parties to discuss the ​crises ‌in ‌the Middle East ‌and Ukraine and their consequences on the energy market.</strong></p><p>The meeting will ‌be held on Friday morning at 10:30am local time on Thursday (that’s 9:30am UK) and military and <strong>intelligence officers will share ⁠the information they have ​provided to ​Macron</strong>, his ​office said ​in ‌a ​statement.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/sep/17/donald-trump-eu-european-union-mark-carney-canada-associate-membership-tariffs-threats-germany-merz-latest-news-updates\">Continue reading...</a>",
